---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | ScamPrep"
  description="What ScamPrep collects, who sees it, and the three promises we keep: we never sell your data, we never touch bank accounts, and participants control their own information."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This policy explains what Sawtooth Technologies LLC, doing business as ScamPrep
        (&ldquo;ScamPrep,&rdquo; &ldquo;we&rdquo;), collects on getscamprep.com and in the ScamPrep
        service, and what we do with it. The short version, which the rest of this policy keeps:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>We never sell your information.</strong> Not to advertisers, not to data brokers,
          not to anyone.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>We never access bank accounts or money.</strong> ScamPrep has no connection to any
          participant&rsquo;s financial accounts, and drills never collect real financial
          information.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Participants control their own data.</strong> Anyone enrolled can see, pause, or
          delete what we hold about them &mdash; regardless of who pays.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>If you join the early-access list:</strong> your name, email, which plan you were
        looking at, how you found us (for example, a link from Facebook), and anything you choose to
        tell us &mdash; such as who you hope to enroll or what worries you. Free-text answers are
        read by a person and used only to understand what families need.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>If you book a call:</strong> the scheduling details and answers you provide through
        our booking page (Cal.com).
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>If you subscribe:</strong> billing name, email, and plan, through our payment
        processor Stripe. <strong>We never see or store full card numbers.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>If you are an enrolled participant:</strong> your name, the contact channel you
        consented to (such as an email address), your responses to practice drills (for example,
        whether a drill was reported, ignored, or clicked), coaching interactions, and the progress
        summaries that make up your Resilience Report.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>On the website:</strong> we use Cloudflare Web Analytics, a privacy-respecting,
        cookieless service that counts visits without identifying or tracking you. We do not use
        advertising trackers.
      </p>

      <h2>What drill data is &mdash; and what it is never used for</h2>
      <p>
        Drill responses are educational progress data: they record how training is going, the way a
        language app records completed lessons. We use them to adjust drill difficulty, coach, and
        produce Resilience Reports.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do <strong>not</strong> use drill data to diagnose, screen for, or infer any medical or
        cognitive condition; we do not build health, credit, insurance, or employment profiles; and
        we never share drill data with advertisers, data brokers, insurers, or financial
        institutions.
      </p>

      <h2>Who sees a participant&rsquo;s information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The participant &mdash; always.</strong></li>
        <li>
          <strong>Family members the participant approves</strong> receive the Resilience Report.
          Sharing is a participant choice, revocable at any time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Partner organizations</strong> (such as an advisory practice or community that
          sponsors enrollment) receive <strong>aggregate, anonymized statistics only</strong> &mdash;
          never an individual&rsquo;s drill responses &mdash; unless the participant has expressly
          approved individual sharing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Service providers</strong> who process data on our instructions: Stripe (payments),
          Formspree (forms), Google Workspace (email), Cloudflare (website hosting and analytics),
          Cal.com (scheduling). Each receives only what its job requires.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Legal requirements:</strong> we disclose information if the law compels it, and we
          will tell you when we are permitted to.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it for cross-context behavioral
        advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Early-access list entries: until launch or until you ask to be removed. Subscriber and
        participant data: for the life of the subscription and up to 12 months after, then deleted
        or anonymized &mdash; sooner on request. Aggregate statistics that identify no one may be
        retained.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>
        Anyone &mdash; participant, subscriber, or list member &mdash; can email
        <a href="mailto:hello@getscamprep.com">hello@getscamprep.com</a> to: see what we hold about
        them, correct it, delete it, or withdraw from drills or emails. Participants can also stop
        drills directly from any drill message. We honor these requests regardless of which state
        you live in, and we respond within 30 days. We will never treat you differently for
        exercising them.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        Data lives in access-controlled systems (Google Workspace, Stripe, Formspree, Cloudflare)
        protected by strong authentication, and we follow the principle of least access. No system
        is perfectly secure; if a breach affects your data, we will notify you promptly as the law
        requires.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        The Site and Service are not directed at anyone under 18, and we do not knowingly collect
        children&rsquo;s data.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we materially change this policy, we will email subscribers and post the change here at
        least 30 days before it takes effect. We will never retroactively weaken the three promises
        at the top without your consent.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Sawtooth Technologies LLC (d/b/a ScamPrep)<br />
        c/o Northwest Registered Agent LLC<br />
        418 Broadway, Ste N<br />
        Albany, NY 12207<br />
        <a href="mailto:hello@getscamprep.com">hello@getscamprep.com</a>
      </p>

      <p class="footnote">Effective date: August 9, 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
